# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$: the same workflow on a 40-qubit register {#44mathrmti-the-same-workflow-on-a-40-qubit-register}"
msgstr "$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$: aliran kerja yang sama pada register 40-qubit {#44mathrmti-the-same-workflow-on-a-40-qubit-register}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $pf$ shell above $^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ has four orbitals per species and 20 magnetic substates each,\n"
"so the register is 40 qubits. Two valence protons and two valence neutrons make $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$,\n"
"with 4,000 symmetry-allowed determinants &mdash; about six times the $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ basis, using\n"
"40 qubits instead of 24.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cengkerang $pf$ di atas $^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ mempunyai empat orbital bagi setiap spesies dan 20 substat magnetik setiap satu,\n"
"jadi register ialah 40 qubit. Dua proton valens dan dua neutron valens membentuk $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$,\n"
"dengan 4,000 penentu yang dibenarkan-simetri &mdash; kira-kira enam kali ganda asas $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, menggunakan\n"
"40 qubit dan bukannya 24.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the larger of the two examples that the notebook can solve exactly, so you can compare\n"
"the hardware result with an exact reference.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini ialah yang lebih besar daripada dua contoh yang boleh diselesaikan secara tepat oleh notebook, jadi anda boleh membandingkan\n"
"hasil perkakasan dengan rujukan tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$: beyond the tutorial's exact-diagonalization capacity {#48mathrmcr-beyond-the-tutorials-exact-diagonalization-capacity}"
msgstr "$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$: melangkaui kapasiti diagonalisasi-tepat tutorial ini {#48mathrmcr-beyond-the-tutorials-exact-diagonalization-capacity}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Adding two protons and two neutrons uses the same 40-qubit register (`4, 4` for\n"
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$) and increases the basis size by a factor of about 491, to 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed determinants. That\n"
"matrix is far beyond anything this tutorial will build, so `exact=False`: there is no exact reference energy,\n"
"only the variational bound and the reference determinant it improves on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menambah dua proton dan dua neutron menggunakan register 40-qubit yang sama (`4, 4` untuk\n"
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$) dan meningkatkan saiz asas dengan faktor kira-kira 491, kepada 1,963,461 penentu yang dibenarkan-simetri. Matriks\n"
"itu jauh melangkaui apa-apa yang akan dibina tutorial ini, jadi `exact=False`: tiada tenaga rujukan tepat,\n"
"hanya sempadan variasional dan penentu rujukan yang diperbaikinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two things change at this scale, and both are visible in the printout. The pool grows to several\n"
"hundred allowed excitations, so the fixed gate budget now covers a minority of it rather than all of\n"
"it. Also, the product subspace the samples span is larger than `MAX_DIMENSION`, so the dense solver\n"
"truncates it by sampled weight. The bound remains rigorous but can be less accurate than a bound\n"
"computed from all the sampled configurations. A production calculation would retain the samples\n"
"and use a solver that supports a larger subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua perkara berubah pada skala ini, dan kedua-duanya kelihatan dalam cetakan. Kolam membesar kepada beberapa\n"
"ratus pengujaan yang dibenarkan, jadi belanjawan get tetap kini merangkumi minoriti daripadanya dan bukan\n"
"keseluruhannya. Selain itu, subruang produk yang direntangi oleh sampel adalah lebih besar daripada `MAX_DIMENSION`, jadi penyelesai tumpat\n"
"memangkasnya mengikut berat sampel. Sempadan itu kekal tegar tetapi mungkin kurang tepat berbanding sempadan\n"
"yang dikira daripada semua konfigurasi yang disampel. Pengiraan pengeluaran akan mengekalkan sampel\n"
"dan menggunakan penyelesai yang menyokong subruang yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate a result without an exact reference {#evaluate-a-result-without-an-exact-reference}"
msgstr "Nilaikan hasil tanpa rujukan tepat {#evaluate-a-result-without-an-exact-reference}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ run has no exact reference within this tutorial. Use the existing samples\n"
"to assess convergence and compare with the classical selection baseline, without additional QPU\n"
"time or full-space diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Larian $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ tiada rujukan tepat dalam tutorial ini. Gunakan sampel sedia ada\n"
"untuk menilai penumpuan dan bandingkan dengan garis dasar pemilihan klasik, tanpa masa QPU\n"
"tambahan atau diagonalisasi ruang-penuh.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Is it converged?** Reorder the retained determinants by their weight in the converged eigenvector\n"
"and the subspaces become *nested*, so diagonalizing the leading $d \\times d$ block for a ladder of $d$\n"
"traces the bound's descent across two decades of subspace size. If it is still falling steeply at the\n"
"largest $d$, the classical solver's dimension cap is the binding constraint and `MAX_DIMENSION` is the\n"
"parameter to increase. If it has flattened, adding more of the retained determinants offers little improvement;\n"
"further progress may require sampling additional configurations. The\n"
"Hamiltonian is built once at full size and every rung is a principal block of it, so the whole\n"
"sweep costs one matrix build rather than one per rung.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Adakah ia sudah menumpu?** Susun semula penentu yang dikekalkan mengikut beratnya dalam eigenvektor yang menumpu\n"
"dan subruang menjadi *bersarang*, jadi mendiagonalisasi blok $d \\times d$ terkemuka bagi tangga $d$\n"
"menjejaki penurunan sempadan merentas dua dekad saiz subruang. Jika ia masih menurun secara mendadak pada\n"
"$d$ terbesar, had dimensi penyelesai klasik ialah kekangan pengikat dan `MAX_DIMENSION` ialah\n"
"parameter yang perlu ditingkatkan. Jika ia telah mendatar, menambah lebih banyak penentu yang dikekalkan hanya memberikan sedikit penambahbaikan;\n"
"kemajuan selanjutnya mungkin memerlukan pensampelan konfigurasi tambahan. Hamiltonian\n"
"dibina sekali sahaja pada saiz penuh dan setiap anak tangga ialah blok utama daripadanya, jadi seluruh\n"
"pengimbasan hanya memerlukan satu pembinaan matriks dan bukan satu bagi setiap anak tangga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**How does quantum sampling compare with classical selection?** Compare with a subspace of the\n"
"same size chosen by the classical selection procedure: take the pool ranked by perturbation theory in score\n"
"order, grow the product subspace to the same dimension, and diagonalize that instead. Both curves are\n"
"rigorous upper bounds on the same Hamiltonian, so whichever sits lower at equal dimension picked the\n"
"better determinants. This comparison decides whether hardware sampling improves the energy estimate\n"
"relative to this classical baseline.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Bagaimana pensampelan kuantum berbanding dengan pemilihan klasik?** Bandingkan dengan subruang yang bersaiz\n"
"sama yang dipilih oleh prosedur pemilihan klasik: ambil kolam yang disusun mengikut teori gangguan dalam susunan skor,\n"
"besarkan subruang produk kepada dimensi yang sama, dan diagonalisasikannya sebaliknya. Kedua-dua lengkung adalah\n"
"sempadan atas tegar bagi Hamiltonian yang sama, jadi mana-mana yang lebih rendah pada dimensi yang sama memilih\n"
"penentu yang lebih baik. Perbandingan ini menentukan sama ada pensampelan perkakasan meningkatkan anggaran tenaga\n"
"berbanding garis dasar klasik ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This subspace is not selected for excited states. Configuration recovery steers the subspace\n"
"using ground-state occupancies, so the higher eigenvalues are much further from converged than the\n"
"lowest one, and the first excitation energy comes out well above the measured $2^+$. Reaching excited\n"
"states properly needs a subspace selected for them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Subruang ini tidak dipilih untuk keadaan teruja. Pemulihan konfigurasi mengarahkan subruang\n"
"menggunakan kependudukan keadaan-dasar, jadi nilai eigen yang lebih tinggi jauh lebih tidak menumpu daripada\n"
"yang terendah, dan tenaga pengujaan pertama datang jauh melebihi $2^+$ yang diukur. Untuk mencapai keadaan\n"
"teruja dengan betul memerlukan subruang yang dipilih khusus untuknya.\n"

