# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background (Fortran) {#background-fortran}"
msgstr "Latar belakang (Fortran) {#background-fortran}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The nuclear shell model treats a nucleus as a few *valence* nucleons moving in a small set of single-particle orbitals above an inert *core*, interacting through an empirical two-body force fitted to measured spectra. Its computational cost is combinatorial: the basis is every way of distributing the valence protons and neutrons over the available states, and this growth limits the model spaces accessible to exact diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Model cengkerang nuklear menganggap nukleus sebagai beberapa nukleon *valens* yang bergerak dalam satu set kecil\n"
"orbital zarah-tunggal di atas *teras* lengai, berinteraksi melalui daya dua-jasad empirik\n"
"yang dipadankan dengan spektrum yang diukur. Kos pengkomputerannya ialah\n"
"kombinatorik: asasnya ialah setiap cara mengagihkan proton dan neutron valens ke atas\n"
"keadaan yang tersedia, dan pertumbuhan ini mengehadkan ruang model yang boleh dicapai oleh pepenjuruan tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pooled sample-based quantum diagonalization (pooled SQD) [\\[1\\]](#references) splits that problem in two. A quantum circuit is used only to *propose* which basis states matter. It is measured in the computational basis, and each measured bitstring names one Slater determinant. The Hamiltonian is then built and diagonalized classically in the span of those determinants. Because the classical step is an exact diagonalization inside a subspace, it returns a variational upper bound on the true ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pepenjuruan kuantum berasaskan sampel terkumpul (SQD terkumpul) [\\[1\\]](#references) membahagikan masalah itu kepada dua. Satu\n"
"litar kuantum digunakan hanya untuk *mencadangkan* keadaan asas yang penting. Ia diukur dalam\n"
"asas pengkomputeran, dan setiap rentetan-bit yang diukur menamakan satu penentu Slater. Hamiltonian\n"
"kemudiannya dibina dan dipenjurukan secara klasik dalam rentang penentu tersebut. Oleh kerana langkah\n"
"klasik ialah pepenjuruan tepat dalam subruang, ia mengembalikan sempadan atas variasional\n"
"bagi tenaga keadaan-asas sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise changes *which* determinants the circuit proposes, but it does not enter the classical Hamiltonian. A shot that violates a conserved quantity is discarded, and a shot that survives is a legitimate basis vector however it was produced. Noise therefore costs subspace quality, not correctness. Nuclear structure provides several exact quantum numbers for this check: a physical determinant must carry the right number of valence protons *and* valence neutrons, the right total angular-momentum projection $M_J$, and the right parity.\n"
msgstr "Hingar mengubah determinan *mana* yang dicadangkan oleh litar, tetapi ia tidak memasuki Hamiltonian klasik. Satu tembakan yang melanggar kuantiti terabadi dibuang, dan tembakan yang terselamat ialah vektor asas yang sah walau bagaimana ia dihasilkan. Oleh itu, hingar menjejaskan kualiti subruang, bukan ketepatan. Struktur nuklear menyediakan beberapa nombor kuantum tepat untuk semakan ini: determinan fizikal mesti membawa bilangan proton valens *dan* neutron valens yang betul, unjuran momentum sudut jumlah $M_J$ yang betul, dan pariti yang betul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran application uses the same register as the Python example. Every qubit is one $m$-scheme single-particle state $(n, \\ell, j, m_j, t_z)$, and $|1\\rangle$ means occupied. Protons come first, then neutrons; within a species, orbitals follow the order of the interaction file; within an orbital, $m_j$ descends. The $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ example here uses this 24-qubit $sd$-shell register.\n"
msgstr "Aplikasi Fortran menggunakan daftar yang sama seperti contoh Python. Setiap qubit ialah satu keadaan zarah tunggal skema-$m$ $(n, \\ell, j, m_j, t_z)$, dan $|1\\rangle$ bermaksud diduduki. Proton didahulukan, kemudian neutron; dalam satu spesies, orbital mengikut susunan fail interaksi; dalam satu orbital, $m_j$ menurun. Contoh $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ di sini menggunakan daftar 24-qubit petala-$sd$ ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hamiltonian is a one-body term plus a two-body interaction,\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian ialah terma satu-jasad ditambah interaksi dua-jasad,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{p} \\varepsilon_p\\, a_p^\\dagger a_p\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sum_{pqrs} \\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle\\, a_p^\\dagger a_q^\\dagger a_s a_r ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{p} \\varepsilon_p\\, a_p^\\dagger a_p\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sum_{pqrs} \\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle\\, a_p^\\dagger a_q^\\dagger a_s a_r ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $p,q,r,s$ label $m$-scheme states. The interaction file tabulates two-body matrix elements in the $J$-coupled basis of orbitals, and the application recovers each $m$-scheme element $\\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle$ by Clebsch-Gordan recoupling. The regression test in [Check the workflow locally](#check-the-workflow-locally) confirms that this produces the same Hamiltonian as the Python example.\n"
msgstr "di mana $p,q,r,s$ melabelkan keadaan skema-$m$. Fail interaksi menjadualkan unsur matriks dua-jasad dalam asas orbital berganding-$J$, dan aplikasi memulihkan setiap unsur skema-$m$ $\\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle$ melalui penggandingan semula Clebsch-Gordan. Ujian regresi dalam [Semak aliran kerja secara tempatan](#check-the-workflow-locally) mengesahkan bahawa ini menghasilkan Hamiltonian yang sama seperti contoh Python.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran workflow {#the-fortran-workflow}"
msgstr "Aliran kerja Fortran {#the-fortran-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reference determinant.** Fill the lowest single-particle-energy $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs of each species, which gives $M_J = 0$.\n"
msgstr "**Determinan rujukan.** Isi pasangan $(+m_j, -m_j)$ tenaga zarah tunggal terendah bagi setiap spesies, yang memberikan $M_J = 0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Excitation pool.** Generate the single and double excitations of the reference allowed by angular-momentum coupling, rank them by a second-order perturbation-theory score, $V^2/|\\Delta|$, and seed each with its two-level mixing angle.\n"
msgstr "**Kolam pengujaan.** Hasilkan pengujaan tunggal dan berganda bagi rujukan yang dibenarkan oleh penggandingan momentum sudut, susun mengikut skor teori gangguan peringkat-kedua, $V^2/|\\Delta|$, dan benihkan setiap satu dengan sudut pencampuran dua-arasnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuit ensemble.** Each circuit prepares the reference and applies the next slice of the ranked pool: Givens rotations for single excitations and qubit-excitation gates for double excitations. With the default of 16 excitations per circuit, 11 circuits cover the whole double-excitation pool for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$.\n"
msgstr "**Ensembel litar.** Setiap litar menyediakan rujukan dan menerapkan hirisan seterusnya bagi kolam yang disusun: putaran Givens untuk pengujaan tunggal dan Gate pengujaan-qubit untuk pengujaan berganda. Dengan lalai 16 pengujaan setiap litar, 11 litar meliputi keseluruhan kolam pengujaan berganda bagi $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sample.** Transpile each circuit and sample it on a QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Sampel.** Transpile setiap litar dan sampelkannya pada QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Filter.** Keep only shots with the right proton number, neutron number, $M_J$, and parity, and discard the rest.\n"
msgstr "**Tapis.** Simpan hanya tembakan dengan bilangan proton, bilangan neutron, $M_J$, dan pariti yang betul, dan buang selebihnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Diagonalize.** Build the Hamiltonian in the span of the unique kept determinants, pooled across all circuits, and diagonalize it with LAPACK to get a variational upper bound. Alternatively, diagonalize each circuit's samples separately.\n"
msgstr "**Pepenjuruan.** Bina Hamiltonian dalam rentang determinan unik yang disimpan, dikumpulkan merentasi semua litar, dan pepenjurukannya dengan LAPACK untuk mendapatkan batas atas variasional. Sebagai alternatif, pepenjurukan sampel setiap litar secara berasingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each step maps to a source file in the Fortran directory:\n"
msgstr "Setiap langkah dipetakan kepada fail sumber dalam direktori Fortran:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Step | Source |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Read the interaction and recouple to the $m$-scheme | `physics/usdb_reader.f90`, `physics/clebsch_gordan.f90`, `physics/orbital_registry.f90` |\n"
"| Rank and seed the excitation pool | `nuclear_pool.f90`, `nuclear_selection.f90` |\n"
"| Build the circuits | `circuit/nuclear_ansatz.f90`, `nuclear_gates.f90` |\n"
"| Sample, filter, and diagonalize | `circuit/nuclear_shell_driver.f90`, `physics/symmetry_filter.f90`, `physics/exact_solver.f90` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Langkah | Sumber |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Baca interaksi dan gandingkan semula kepada skema-$m$ | `physics/usdb_reader.f90`, `physics/clebsch_gordan.f90`, `physics/orbital_registry.f90` |\n"
"| Susun dan semai kumpulan pengujaan | `nuclear_pool.f90`, `nuclear_selection.f90` |\n"
"| Bina litar | `circuit/nuclear_ansatz.f90`, `nuclear_gates.f90` |\n"
"| Sampel, tapis, dan pepenjurukan | `circuit/nuclear_shell_driver.f90`, `physics/symmetry_filter.f90`, `physics/exact_solver.f90` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran workflow differs from the Python example in several choices, such as how it picks the reference determinant and how it handles samples with the wrong symmetry. [Differences from the Python example](#differences-from-the-python-example) lists them.\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja Fortran berbeza daripada contoh Python dalam beberapa pilihan, seperti cara ia memilih penentu rujukan dan cara ia mengendalikan sampel yang mempunyai simetri yang salah. [Perbezaan daripada contoh Python](#differences-from-the-python-example) menyenaraikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements (Fortran) {#requirements-fortran}"
msgstr "Keperluan (Fortran) {#requirements-fortran}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This implementation is adapted from the nuclear shell-model application in [qiskit-fortran](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-fortran), the Fortran bindings for Qiskit. Build and run the version in the Fortran directory linked in the preceding note rather than the upstream application, because it includes corrections to interaction mass scaling and antisymmetrized pair-exchange phases.\n"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan ini diadaptasi daripada aplikasi model petala nuklear dalam [qiskit-fortran](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-fortran), iaitu ikatan Fortran untuk Qiskit. Bina dan jalankan versi dalam direktori Fortran yang dipautkan dalam nota sebelum ini, bukannya aplikasi huluan, kerana ia termasuk pembetulan untuk penskalaan jisim interaksi dan fasa pertukaran pasangan antisimetri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow the [build instructions](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/nuclear_sqd_pooled/fortran/BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md) to build the Qiskit C library, the Fortran bindings, and this application. The build instructions set `NUCLEAR_SRC` to the Fortran directory and `NUCLEAR_DEPS` to a separate directory for the dependencies; the commands in this example use those variables. Use the same Fortran compiler for the bindings and the application, because module files are compiler-specific. Building the Qiskit C library (`make c`) takes several minutes.\n"
msgstr "Ikuti [arahan pembinaan](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/nuclear_sqd_pooled/fortran/BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md) untuk membina pustaka C Qiskit, ikatan Fortran, dan aplikasi ini. Arahan pembinaan menetapkan `NUCLEAR_SRC` kepada direktori Fortran dan `NUCLEAR_DEPS` kepada direktori berasingan untuk kebergantungan; arahan dalam contoh ini menggunakan pemboleh ubah tersebut. Gunakan pengkompil Fortran yang sama untuk ikatan dan aplikasi, kerana fail modul adalah khusus kepada pengkompil. Membina pustaka C Qiskit (`make c`) mengambil masa beberapa minit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Quantum Compute Client support described in the build instructions is optional. You need it only to submit hardware jobs; the local checks and saved-bitstring processing work without it.\n"
msgstr "Sokongan Quantum Compute Client yang diterangkan dalam arahan pembinaan adalah pilihan. Anda hanya memerlukannya untuk menghantar kerja perkakasan; semakan setempat dan pemprosesan rentetan bit yang disimpan berfungsi tanpanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The build produces `nuclear_shell_driver` in `$NUCLEAR_SRC/build` and copies `data/USDB.snt` beside it. Despite its filename, that file contains the **USDA** interaction, as its header states. The supplied example describes two valence protons and two valence neutrons in the $sd$ shell, which is $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, the same nucleus as the Python small-scale hardware example.\n"
msgstr "Pembinaan menghasilkan `nuclear_shell_driver` dalam `$NUCLEAR_SRC/build` dan menyalin `data/USDB.snt` di sebelahnya. Walaupun namanya begitu, fail itu mengandungi interaksi **USDA**, seperti yang dinyatakan pada pengepalanya. Contoh yang dibekalkan menerangkan dua proton valens dan dua neutron valens dalam petala $sd$, iaitu $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, nukleus yang sama seperti contoh perkakasan berskala kecil Python.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the workflow locally {#check-the-workflow-locally}"
msgstr "Semak aliran kerja secara setempat {#check-the-workflow-locally}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, run the Hamiltonian regression test:\n"
msgstr "Pertama, jalankan ujian regresi Hamiltonian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The test builds the complete 640-determinant basis for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, diagonalizes it, and checks that the ground-state energy is $-40.472331$ MeV, the exact energy in the Python example. Passing confirms that the Fortran application builds the same Hamiltonian as the Python example. Because SQD diagonalizes in a subspace of this basis, no run of this application can report an energy below $-40.472331$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$; the closer a run gets, the better its sampled subspace.\n"
msgstr "Ujian ini membina asas 640 penentu yang lengkap untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, memepenjurukannya, dan menyemak bahawa tenaga keadaan asas ialah $-40.472331$ MeV, iaitu tenaga tepat dalam contoh Python. Lulus bermakna aplikasi Fortran membina Hamiltonian yang sama seperti contoh Python. Oleh sebab SQD memepenjurukan dalam subruang asas ini, tiada larian aplikasi ini yang boleh melaporkan tenaga di bawah $-40.472331$ MeV untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$; semakin dekat larian itu, semakin baik subruang yang disampelnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, run the driver without hardware from the build directory:\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, jalankan pemacu tanpa perkakasan dari direktori pembinaan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without `--runtime`, the application generates copies of the reference determinant rather than sampling a simulated quantum circuit. This checks the classical filtering and diagonalization pipeline; it does not test circuit sampling. The selected subspace has dimension one, so its energy is the reference determinant's diagonal matrix element.\n"
msgstr "Tanpa `--runtime`, aplikasi menjana salinan penentu rujukan dan bukannya mensampel litar kuantum yang disimulasikan. Ini menyemak saluran paip penapisan dan pepenjurukan klasik; ia tidak menguji persampelan litar. Subruang yang dipilih mempunyai dimensi satu, jadi tenaganya ialah unsur matriks pepenjuru penentu rujukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The run prints a detailed log. The expected result is in the `RESULT` lines near the end:\n"
msgstr "Larian ini mencetak log terperinci. Keputusan yang dijangkakan terdapat dalam baris `RESULT` berhampiran penghujung:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To check saved-bitstring processing, run:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyemak pemprosesan rentetan bit yang disimpan, jalankan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second command reads the `bitstrings_stepNN.txt` files written by the first, without submitting hardware jobs. Its `per-step` mode diagonalizes each file separately; it does not combine all files into one pooled subspace. `per-step` is the default with `--bitstrings-dir`, and `--mode pooled` is rejected there, because pooled mode runs the full circuit ensemble. Saved samples, including those from a hardware run, can therefore only be reprocessed per step.\n"
msgstr "Arahan kedua membaca fail `bitstrings_stepNN.txt` yang ditulis oleh arahan pertama, tanpa menghantar kerja perkakasan. Mod `per-step`nya memepenjurukan setiap fail secara berasingan; ia tidak menggabungkan semua fail menjadi satu subruang terkumpul. `per-step` ialah lalai dengan `--bitstrings-dir`, dan `--mode pooled` ditolak di situ, kerana mod pooled menjalankan keseluruhan ensembel litar. Sampel yang disimpan, termasuk daripada larian perkakasan, oleh itu hanya boleh diproses semula mengikut langkah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware {#run-on-hardware}"
msgstr "Jalankan pada perkakasan {#run-on-hardware}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These commands assume you have already [saved your IBM Quantum Platform credentials locally](/guides/save-credentials). The pinned Quantum Compute client reads `~/.qiskit/qiskit-ibm.json`; use an account named `default`, `default-ibm-quantum-platform`, or `default-ibm-cloud`. Do not put API keys in tutorial files.\n"
msgstr "Arahan ini menganggap anda sudah [menyimpan bukti kelayakan IBM Quantum Platform anda secara setempat](/guides/save-credentials). Klien Quantum Compute yang disematkan membaca `~/.qiskit/qiskit-ibm.json`; gunakan akaun bernama `default`, `default-ibm-quantum-platform`, atau `default-ibm-cloud`. Jangan letakkan kunci API dalam fail tutorial.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From `$NUCLEAR_SRC/build`, run:\n"
msgstr "Dari `$NUCLEAR_SRC/build`, jalankan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a backend available to your account with enough qubits for the model space; without `--backend`, the driver uses the least-busy backend. The driver transpiles each circuit, submits it as its own Sampler job, and waits for that job to finish before building the next circuit. The command shown therefore runs 11 jobs one after another, each with 4,096 shots on a 24-qubit register, and uses QPU time for each. If a job does not complete, the driver skips it and leaves its samples out of the pool. The driver also writes the returned samples to `bitstrings_stepNN.txt` files, which you can reprocess per step as shown in the previous section. Counts and energies depend on the samples and device noise.\n"
msgstr "Pilih backend yang tersedia untuk akaun anda dengan bilangan qubit yang mencukupi untuk ruang model; tanpa `--backend`, pemacu menggunakan backend yang paling kurang sibuk. Pemacu mentranspil setiap litar, menghantarnya sebagai kerja Sampler tersendiri, dan menunggu kerja itu selesai sebelum membina litar seterusnya. Oleh itu arahan yang ditunjukkan menjalankan 11 kerja satu demi satu, masing-masing dengan 4,096 tembakan pada daftar 24 qubit, dan menggunakan masa QPU untuk setiap satu. Jika sesuatu kerja tidak selesai, pemacu melangkaunya dan tidak memasukkan sampelnya ke dalam kumpulan. Pemacu juga menulis sampel yang dikembalikan ke fail `bitstrings_stepNN.txt`, yang boleh anda proses semula mengikut langkah seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam bahagian sebelumnya. Kiraan dan tenaga bergantung pada sampel dan hingar peranti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `./nuclear_shell_driver --help` for the full option list. To use another interaction, supply `--snt /absolute/path/to/interaction.snt` and the corresponding valence nucleon counts. Only the $sd$-shell interaction is included; `--shell pf` requires a separately supplied `gxpf1.snt` file.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan `./nuclear_shell_driver --help` untuk senarai pilihan penuh. Untuk menggunakan interaksi lain, bekalkan `--snt /absolute/path/to/interaction.snt` dan bilangan nukleon valens yang sepadan. Hanya interaksi petala $sd$ disertakan; `--shell pf` memerlukan fail `gxpf1.snt` yang dibekalkan secara berasingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
