#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix {#appendix}"
msgstr "Lampiran {#appendix}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section explains the reasoning behind the helpers introduced in the [Setup](#setup) section.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian ini menerangkan sebab di sebalik pembantu yang diperkenalkan dalam bahagian [Persediaan](#setup).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the mass-dependence rescaling is not optional {#why-the-mass-dependence-rescaling-is-not-optional}"
msgstr "Mengapa penskalaan semula pergantungan-jisim tidak pilihan {#why-the-mass-dependence-rescaling-is-not-optional}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Empirical shell-model interactions are fitted at one mass and applied across a chain of isotopes, with\n"
"the two-body matrix elements scaled as $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{p}$. Both interaction files carry\n"
"$p = -0.3$, with $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ for the USD family and $42$ for GXPF1. Note that on the two-body header\n"
"line of a `.snt` file, those two numbers sit where an oscillator frequency and a core energy would\n"
"plausibly go, which makes them easy to misread; reading the exponent as a constant core energy adds a\n"
"spurious offset to every diagonal element *and* drops the rescaling, changing the correlation energy by\n"
"a few percent. The symmetry check in Step 1 does not by itself verify the energy scale. Comparing\n"
"the $2^+$ excitation energy, measured in MeV, with experiment provides an additional check on the\n"
"mass-dependent rescaling. An excitation energy is a difference between levels, so it does not\n"
"detect a constant offset applied to all energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Interaksi model-cengkerang empirikal dipadankan pada satu jisim dan diaplikasikan merentas rantaian isotop, dengan\n"
"unsur matriks dua-badan diskalakan sebagai $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{p}$. Kedua-dua fail interaksi membawa\n"
"$p = -0.3$, dengan $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ bagi keluarga USD dan $42$ bagi GXPF1. Perhatikan bahawa pada baris pengepala\n"
"dua-badan sesebuah fail `.snt`, kedua-dua nombor itu terletak di tempat frekuensi osilator dan tenaga teras\n"
"secara munasabah boleh berada, yang menjadikannya mudah disalah baca; membaca eksponen sebagai tenaga teras malar menambah\n"
"ofset palsu kepada setiap unsur pepenjuru *dan* menggugurkan penskalaan semula, mengubah tenaga korelasi sebanyak\n"
"beberapa peratus. Semakan simetri dalam Langkah 1 tidak dengan sendirinya mengesahkan skala tenaga.\n"
"Membandingkan tenaga pengujaan $2^+$, yang diukur dalam MeV, dengan eksperimen memberikan semakan tambahan pada\n"
"penskalaan semula bergantung-jisim. Tenaga pengujaan ialah perbezaan antara paras, jadi ia tidak\n"
"mengesan ofset malar yang dikenakan pada semua tenaga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the reference is found by search rather than by filling {#why-the-reference-is-found-by-search-rather-than-by-filling}"
msgstr "Mengapa rujukan dicari melalui carian dan bukan melalui pengisian {#why-the-reference-is-found-by-search-rather-than-by-filling}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The obvious reference is the determinant that fills the lowest single-particle energies. It is not the\n"
"lowest-energy determinant, because the diagonal of Equation (1) includes the two-body term\n"
"$\\sum_{i<j} \\langle ij \\| ij \\rangle$, and the pairing interaction strongly prefers occupying\n"
"time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ partners in the *largest* available $|m_j|$. In the $sd$ shell, that is the\n"
"difference between the $m_j = \\pm 1/2$ pair and the $m_j = \\pm 5/2$ pair of $0d_{5/2}$, and it is worth\n"
"about 1 MeV; in the $pf$ shell, it is worth closer to 2. Because the reference energy defines the zero of the\n"
"\"correlation energy recovered\" metric, a poor choice inflates that metric and gives a less accurate\n"
"starting point.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rujukan yang jelas ialah penentu yang mengisi tenaga zarah-tunggal terendah. Ia bukan penentu\n"
"tenaga-terendah, kerana pepenjuru Persamaan (1) mengandungi terma dua-badan\n"
"$\\sum_{i<j} \\langle ij \\| ij \\rangle$, dan interaksi pemasangan sangat memilih menduduki\n"
"rakan terbalik-masa $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pada $|m_j|$ tersedia yang *terbesar*. Dalam cengkerang $sd$, itu ialah\n"
"perbezaan antara pasangan $m_j = \\pm 1/2$ dan pasangan $m_j = \\pm 5/2$ bagi $0d_{5/2}$, dan bernilai\n"
"kira-kira 1 MeV; dalam cengkerang $pf$, ia bernilai lebih hampir kepada 2. Kerana tenaga rujukan menentukan sifar\n"
"bagi metrik \"tenaga korelasi yang dipulihkan\", pilihan yang buruk menggelembungkan metrik itu dan memberikan titik\n"
"mula yang kurang tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restricting to paired fillings makes exhaustive search inexpensive, with $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ candidates per\n"
"species (a few thousand at most), and ensures $M_J = 0$. In every case in this\n"
"tutorial that can be checked against a full enumeration, the search returns the global lowest-diagonal\n"
"determinant, which is also the single largest component of the exact ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengehadkan kepada pengisian berpasangan menjadikan carian menyeluruh murah, dengan $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ calon bagi setiap\n"
"spesies (paling banyak beberapa ribu), dan memastikan $M_J = 0$. Dalam setiap kes dalam tutorial ini\n"
"yang boleh disemak terhadap penyenaraian penuh, carian mengembalikan penentu pepenjuru-terendah global,\n"
"yang juga merupakan komponen tunggal terbesar bagi keadaan dasar tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the first-order amplitude, not the exact two-level angle {#why-the-first-order-amplitude-not-the-exact-two-level-angle}"
msgstr "Mengapa amplitud peringkat-pertama, bukan sudut dua-paras yang tepat {#why-the-first-order-amplitude-not-the-exact-two-level-angle}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diagonalizing the $2 \\times 2$ Hamiltonian in the space\n"
"$\\{|\\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}}\\rangle, |\\alpha\\rangle\\}$ gives the mixing angle\n"
"$\\theta_{\\mathrm{exact}} = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2V/\\Delta)$; it might be tempting to call that the correct\n"
"choice for an *isolated* pair of levels. In this ansatz, several dozen excitation blocks act\n"
"in sequence on the same reference, so optimizing each block separately does not necessarily\n"
"optimize the composite circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mendiagonalisasi Hamiltonian $2 \\times 2$ dalam ruang\n"
"$\\{|\\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}}\\rangle, |\\alpha\\rangle\\}$ memberikan sudut percampuran\n"
"$\\theta_{\\mathrm{exact}} = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2V/\\Delta)$; mungkin menggoda untuk menyebut itu pilihan yang betul\n"
"bagi sepasang paras yang *terpencil*. Dalam ansatz ini, beberapa dozen blok pengujaan bertindak\n"
"secara berjujukan pada rujukan yang sama, jadi mengoptimumkan setiap blok secara berasingan tidak semestinya\n"
"mengoptimumkan litar komposit.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit's role determines the choice of angle. Since\n"
"$|\\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2x)| \\le |x|$ for every real $x$, the exact angle is always *smaller* in\n"
"magnitude than the first-order amplitude $t = V/\\Delta$, and therefore always leaves *more* amplitude\n"
"on the reference determinant. A circuit that keeps more amplitude on the reference returns the\n"
"reference more often and distinct excited determinants less often. For pooled SQD, the useful output of a shot\n"
"is a determinant the classical step has not seen yet, which motivates using the larger angle in this tutorial. Neither angle needs to be accurate, because the classical diagonalization discards the circuit's\n"
"amplitudes entirely and re-derives its own.\n"
msgstr ""
"Peranan litar menentukan pilihan sudut. Kerana\n"
"$|\\tfrac{1}{2}\\arctan(2x)| \\le |x|$ bagi setiap $x$ nyata, sudut tepat sentiasa *lebih kecil* dalam\n"
"magnitud berbanding amplitud peringkat-pertama $t = V/\\Delta$, dan oleh itu sentiasa meninggalkan *lebih banyak* amplitud\n"
"pada penentu rujukan. Litar yang mengekalkan lebih banyak amplitud pada rujukan mengembalikan rujukan\n"
"lebih kerap dan penentu teruja yang berbeza lebih jarang. Bagi SQD berkumpul, output berguna bagi satu shot\n"
"ialah penentu yang belum dilihat oleh langkah klasik, yang mendorong penggunaan sudut yang lebih besar dalam tutorial ini. Tiada satu sudut pun perlu tepat, kerana diagonalisasi klasik membuang amplitud litar\n"
"sepenuhnya dan mendapatkan semula amplitudnya sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why pooled SQD can use qubit excitations {#why-pooled-sqd-can-use-qubit-excitations}"
msgstr "Mengapa SQD berkumpul boleh menggunakan pengujaan qubit {#why-pooled-sqd-can-use-qubit-excitations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fermionic excitation $T = a_{v_1}^\\dagger a_{v_2}^\\dagger a_{h_2} a_{h_1}$ maps under\n"
"Jordan-Wigner to eight Pauli strings, each carrying $Z$ operators on every qubit between the outermost\n"
"indices. Those strings encode the fermionic sign, and their cost grows with the span, which for a\n"
"proton-neutron excitation is the whole register.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengujaan fermionik $T = a_{v_1}^\\dagger a_{v_2}^\\dagger a_{h_2} a_{h_1}$ dipetakan di bawah\n"
"Jordan-Wigner kepada lapan rentetan Pauli, setiap satu membawa operator $Z$ pada setiap qubit antara indeks\n"
"terluar. Rentetan itu mengekod tanda fermionik, dan kosnya bertambah dengan jangkauan, yang bagi\n"
"pengujaan proton-neutron ialah keseluruhan register.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deleting them gives the qubit-excitation operator of Yordanov et al. [\\[5\\]](#references). It is a\n"
"different operator: the state it prepares differs from the fermionic one in the *signs* of\n"
"its amplitudes, and the two sampling distributions can differ substantially. What it does not change\n"
"is which determinants have nonzero amplitude, because each block still rotates within the same\n"
"two-dimensional space $\\{|d\\rangle, |d'\\rangle\\}$ for every determinant $d$ it acts on, and it still\n"
"conserves both nucleon numbers, $M_J$, and parity exactly. The reachable set of determinants is\n"
"therefore identical, and the reachable set is the only thing pooled SQD uses; the classical\n"
"diagonalization assigns its own amplitudes regardless. Step 2 verifies the identical-support claim on\n"
"a real operator from the pool and measures what the substitution saves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menghapuskannya memberikan operator pengujaan-qubit Yordanov et al. [\\[5\\]](#references). Ia ialah\n"
"operator yang berbeza: keadaan yang disediakannya berbeza daripada yang fermionik dalam *tanda*\n"
"amplitudnya, dan kedua-dua taburan pensampelan boleh berbeza dengan ketara. Apa yang tidak berubah\n"
"ialah penentu mana yang mempunyai amplitud bukan sifar, kerana setiap blok masih berputar dalam ruang\n"
"dua-dimensi yang sama $\\{|d\\rangle, |d'\\rangle\\}$ bagi setiap penentu $d$ yang ditindaknya, dan ia masih\n"
"mengekalkan kedua-dua bilangan nukleon, $M_J$, dan pariti dengan tepat. Set penentu yang boleh dicapai adalah\n"
"oleh itu sama, dan set yang boleh dicapai itulah satu-satunya perkara yang digunakan SQD berkumpul; diagonalisasi\n"
"klasik menetapkan amplitudnya sendiri tanpa mengira. Langkah 2 mengesahkan dakwaan sokongan-sama pada\n"
"operator sebenar daripada kolam dan mengukur apa yang dijimatkan oleh penggantian itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The limitation is that the sampling *weights* differ, so the two constructions will not discover\n"
"determinants in the same order at finite shot count. Since the ranking that decides which excitations\n"
"enter the circuits is classical and unchanged, and the classical step re-weights everything anyway,\n"
"the difference in sampling weights is a tradeoff for reduced circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Batasannya ialah *berat* pensampelan berbeza, jadi kedua-dua pembinaan tidak akan menemui\n"
"penentu dalam susunan yang sama pada bilangan shot yang terhingga. Kerana kedudukan yang menentukan pengujaan mana\n"
"yang memasuki litar adalah klasik dan tidak berubah, dan langkah klasik itu memberi berat semula segalanya, \n"
"perbezaan dalam berat pensampelan ialah pertukaran demi kedalaman litar yang berkurangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why $M_J$ belongs to the product stage {#why-m-j-belongs-to-the-product-stage}"
msgstr "Mengapa $M_J$ kepunyaan peringkat produk {#why-m-j-belongs-to-the-product-stage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Post-selection and configuration recovery both act on Hamming weights: the number of protons in one\n"
"half of the register, and the number of neutrons in the other. $M_J = M_p + M_n$ is not of that form. It is a property of a proton configuration *paired with* a neutron configuration. A shot whose proton\n"
"half and neutron half each carry the right nucleon number contains two usable half-configurations even\n"
"when their $M_J$ values do not cancel, because the proton half at $M_p = +1$ is perfectly good once it\n"
"is paired with a neutron half at $M_n = -1$. Filtering whole shots on total $M_J$ throws both halves\n"
"away, and imposing $M_J$ on the recombined products keeps them. The same argument explains why\n"
"`recover_configurations` needs no notion of $M_J$ to be useful in this case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pasca-pemilihan dan pemulihan konfigurasi kedua-duanya bertindak pada berat Hamming: bilangan proton dalam satu\n"
"separuh register, dan bilangan neutron dalam separuh yang lain. $M_J = M_p + M_n$ bukan dalam bentuk itu.\n"
"Ia ialah ciri konfigurasi proton *dipasangkan dengan* konfigurasi neutron. Satu shot yang separuh protonnya\n"
"dan separuh neutronnya masing-masing membawa bilangan nukleon yang betul mengandungi dua separuh-konfigurasi yang boleh digunakan\n"
"walaupun nilai $M_J$ mereka tidak saling membatalkan, kerana separuh proton pada $M_p = +1$ adalah sempurna baik\n"
"sebaik sahaja dipasangkan dengan separuh neutron pada $M_n = -1$. Menapis keseluruhan shot berdasarkan $M_J$ jumlah membuang\n"
"kedua-dua separuh itu, dan mengenakan $M_J$ pada produk yang digabung semula mengekalkannya. Hujah yang sama menerangkan mengapa\n"
"`recover_configurations` tidak memerlukan sebarang konsep $M_J$ untuk berguna dalam kes ini.\n"

